  {
    "id": "matchup.dancer_rush",
    "name": "Jotaro and Kakyoin vs the Blade Dancer and the Iron Brawler",
    "description": "The Blade Dancer's home encounter, and the fixture the Dancer's own numbers were argued against twice before they were argued correctly. Reading one paired the Dancer with the Flame Assassin and measured 100%: removing the Iron Brawler removed the tier's threat, foe output fell from the ambush's 975 per battle to 487, and the party won every seed. Reading two restored the Brawler and measured 95%, because the Dancer at 340 HP took 2.60 actions per battle beside the Brawler against 2.61 beside the Assassin - its lifetime was invariant to its partner, so pairing could not fix it, and the Brawler itself weakened from 631 to 531 because a flimsy ally leaves the survivor alone against the whole party sooner. The Dancer has the highest action rate in the game at 0.137 against the Brawler's 0.058, and delivered 0.65 times the Brawler's actions: 27% of the speed it was built around. Hence 620 HP, which is the Brawler's own figure and puts the foe pool at 1320 against the 1340 the balance curve was measured at, so the curve applies here almost uncorrected. Reading three measured 70% against a predicted 72..86, and the Dancer reached 5.03 actions per battle against a predicted 5.5 or more. Fragility now means def 38, the lowest in the game against subtractive defence, and no longer means a small HP pool; that is a recorded retreat from the brief in #16, which cannot be met against a party as fast as Jotaro and Kakyoin. Band 60..90, unchanged rather than widened across all three readings.",
