  {
    "id": "matchup.weaver_gambit",
    "name": "Jotaro and Kakyoin vs the Hex Weaver and the Iron Brawler",
    "description": "The Hex Weaver's home encounter, and the third fixture built from the ambush by exchanging one foe beside a constant Iron Brawler. The Weaver deals almost nothing itself; its whole contribution is removing party output, which no column in the report can show, so it was read by comparing damage per ACTION against the sibling fixtures rather than by reading the Weaver's own line. That distinction cost three readings to learn: party dealt/b is pinned to the foe HP pool whenever the party usually wins, 1179 against 1180 and 1256 against 1260, so it cannot show a debuff at all, and an early diagnosis that the party was barely being debuffed rested on exactly that column and was wrong. Four readings in total: 92% at hp 480 duration 3, 88% at hp 560 duration 8, 77% at hp 690 duration 8, and 87% at hp 690 duration 3, the last of which was a deliberate single-variable revert that falsified a claim that duration had saturated. Both fields are load-bearing and neither alone was enough - hit points buy the caster turns, duration decides how many of the party's turns those casts reach. The most transferable number from the whole exercise: party damage per party action moved 89.8 to 96.0, only 6.9%, and the win rate moved ten points, so win rate runs about 1.45 points per 1% of party damage per action and every band in this file is more fragile than it looks. Band 58..86, the narrowest here, unchanged across all four readings.",
